{"id": "EUVD-2026-15227", "enisaUuid": "38fc500c-4208-3969-ad24-d5a2cfaa4d01", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\naccel/amdxdna: Fix dead lock for suspend and resume\n\nWhen an application issues a query IOCTL while auto suspend is running,\na deadlock can occur. The query path holds dev_lock and then calls\npm_runtime_resume_and_get(), which waits for the ongoing suspend to\ncomplete. Meanwhile, the suspend callback attempts to acquire dev_lock\nand blocks, resulting in a deadlock.\n\nFix this by releasing dev_lock before calling pm_runtime_resume_and_get()\nand reacquiring it after the call completes. Also acquire dev_lock in the\nresume callback to keep the locking consistent.", "datePublished": "2026-03-25T10:26:52", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T10:06:56", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ac24537478dd8eb2fd3984b4652bb19461e5e74c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1aa82181a3c285c7351523d587f7981ae4c015c8"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-23295"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.09, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "33b690fa-c4e9-3059-887c-4771908f784f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19.7"}, {"id": "6f5e6b33-a8d3-3445-85d9-cd2f4856eb57", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3bdd26582d026bdd86aa76f03989a1137b2490a0"}, {"id": "9049eb62-3574-3dfa-9404-cc9e199f2a11", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "98a86999-328c-3515-a009-a8cf2b27f85e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "063db451832b8849faf1b0b8404b3a6a39995b29 <ac24537478dd8eb2fd3984b4652bb19461e5e74c"}, {"id": "a68470e9-65b1-326e-b71e-476bc9cf1b0d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18.57 <6.19"}, {"id": "bb7bc755-0dd8-3d9c-8086-1d6f49bb8383", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "063db451832b8849faf1b0b8404b3a6a39995b29 <1aa82181a3c285c7351523d587f7981ae4c015c8"}, {"id": "d58f3d32-d7a9-326f-a727-48599091a700", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.19"}, {"id": "e753d50b-6b14-383c-8f5b-4373032d2543", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8ce0e155-6dde-37cc-8fd8-b0ac92cc1fd9", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}